# rhwp script, width and PDF sheet fixes for why-hwp, measured against Hangul 2024 output.
# Base: rhwp 7213ed1f9 after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh and
# wasm/patches/rhwp-layout.patch, rhwp-layout2.patch and rhwp-layout3.patch;
# apply this after rhwp-layout3.patch.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero).
#
# - script_metrics.rs: superscript and subscript size and shift use the Hangul
#   2024 rule (0.64 em size, 0.44 em up, 0.12 em down) for every document but
#   HWP 3.0 ones, which keep the older rule.
# - layout/text_measurement.rs: a bold HFT character outside ASCII that is
#   measured with a known original-font width also takes the HFT bold advance
#   (bold HCI Poppy U+00B7). ASCII keeps its plain advance, as bold HCI Poppy
#   `=` does in Hangul 2024 print.
# - font_metrics_overlays.rs: the 필기 (Pilgi) U+2019 advances 500/1000 em.
# - font_metrics_technical_symbols.rs: Malgun Gothic arrows (U+2190-U+2199,
#   U+21D2, U+21D4) advance 1946/2048 em, as in the font's hmtx.
# - pdf.rs, document_core/queries/rendering.rs, model/document.rs: a document
#   whose print method is 4 (2 pages per sheet) and whose pages are all A4
#   portrait exports to PDF with two pages side by side on a landscape sheet,
#   scaled by 0.71, the left page at x 0, the right one at half the sheet width,
#   both at the top. Links and named destinations move with their page.
# - font_paths.rs, native_webfonts.rs: the 64 MiB font supply budget is kept
#   only when the Skia catalog it is for is built; without Skia every supplied
#   font is kept and host font folders do not use up the budget.
# - svg.rs: the invisible text over a vector U+00B7 is fitted to the glyph-fit
#   advance, as other characters are, instead of the substitute font's width.
# - font_metrics_data.rs, layout/text_measurement.rs, script_metrics.rs,
#   font_paths.rs, pdf.rs, document_core/queries/rendering.rs and svg/tests.rs
#   cover these changes.
